    {
      "id": "c8958083-0690-4ae7-84b1-a75c00ba9c45",
      "name": "1. Start here",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        17888,
        4544
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 916,
        "height": 636,
        "content": "## README\n\nWorkshop scanners retry. Find the first arrival, busiest session and kits still waiting. **Starter, not a finished solution.**\n\n1. Enter your username and participant key in **Settings**.\n2. Use your registered Community Weekly Challenge identity. No staging password is needed.\n3. Run **Start** for case/scans. Add native nodes and connect results; checks start disabled.\n\nSubmit finished JSON with the key blank, no credentials and no pinned data.\n\n[Challenge brief](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/challenge) \u00b7 [FAQ](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/faq) \u00b7 [Submit](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/submit)"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5d837c60-f2c6-470a-9de0-4754ad7a2b89",
      "name": "Stage 1: First through the door",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        18864,
        3872
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 1066,
        "height": 430,
        "content": "## Stage 1 \u00b7 First through the door\n\nFind the attendee with the earliest **ACCEPTED** scan. Timestamps are full UTC instants.\n\nHint: **Filter \u2192 Sort \u2192 Limit**.\n\nConnect your last node to **Stage 1 answer**. Replace its blank `b1` value with an expression from your result. Then enable **Check stage 1** when ready."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "1e4de506-fd37-4786-80cc-dddb3d2545bf",
      "name": "Stage 2: Most popular room",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        18864,
        4320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 1058,
        "height": 618,
        "content": "## Stage 2 \u00b7 Most popular room\n\nCount distinct attendees with an **ACCEPTED** scan in each session. Retry scans are one attendee, and each accepted attendee belongs to one session. The busiest session is unique.\n\nHint: **Filter \u2192 Remove Duplicates \u2192 Summarize \u2192 Sort \u2192 Limit**.\n\nConnect your result to **Stage 2 answer**, set `b2` to your session expression, then run. **Get kits** uses that result."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6bbf5ff9-def4-4786-b2c9-f6fc590113e2",
      "name": "Stage 3: Kits still waiting",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        18864,
        4960
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 1058,
        "height": 406,
        "content": "## Stage 3 \u00b7 Kits still waiting\n\nUse **Kit rows** from the Stage 2 session. Count only **CONFIRMED** attendees who requested a kit and have not picked it up.\n\nHint: combine all three conditions in a **Filter**, then **Summarize** the count.\n\nConnect the count to **Stage 3 answer** and use an expression for `b3`. Enable checks only when ready. Export your finished workflow for the portal submission."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e906b737-bebe-4664-a138-61314d743c25",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        17856,
        3872
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 992,
        "height": 1488,
        "content": "## Challenge 04: The Welcome Desk\n\nAn n8n Community challenge: find the first arrival, the busiest session and the kits still waiting.\n\n**This is a starter, not a finished solution.** Data and checks are available while Challenge 04 is open.\n\n### Get started\n\n1. [Read the brief](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/challenge) and [register](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/register), or use your existing participant key.\n2. Import into your n8n instance. Enter your username and key in **Settings**, keep the production base and HTTP Authentication **None**, then run **Start**.\n3. Build with native nodes and connect your computed results to the answer nodes. Kits use your Stage 2 result. Enable checks when ready.\n4. [Submit](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/submit) your completed workflow JSON, answers and explanation. Blank the key and remove credentials and pinned data before exporting.\n\nNo Code, Function, AI, Agent, MCP or Tool nodes, hardcoded answers or hidden code. **11 points after verification on three unseen datasets.**\n\n### Useful links\n\n- [Home](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/site) \u00b7 [Challenges](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/challenges)\n- [Your account](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/status) \u00b7 [Recover key](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/reset) \u00b7 [FAQ](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/faq)\n- [Results](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/results) \u00b7 [Profiles](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/user)\n- [Learn and practise](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/learn) \u00b7 [n8n Academy](https://learn.n8n.io/)\n- [Challenge help](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/community) \u00b7 [Community forum](https://community.n8n.io/)\n- [n8n](https://n8n.io/) \u00b7 [Documentation](https://docs.n8n.io/)\n\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
